+        # A crate may opt out with tags = ["no-check-output-for-working-dir"], which
+        # crate.annotation already knows how to set, so this needs no new API.
+        #
+        # The check's advice -- stop retaining env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR") or
+        # env!("OUT_DIR") -- assumes the path came from Rust. For a crate that statically
+        # links a C library built from source, it did not: OpenSSL records ENGINESDIR,
+        # MODULESDIR and its full compiler command line into libcrypto.a by design (they
+        # are what `openssl version -a` prints), openssl-sys links that archive, and no
+        # change to any Rust source can remove them. Without an opt-out such a crate is
+        # simply unbuildable.
+        # getattr, not ctx.attr.tags: rustc_compile is reached from the prost aspect too,
+        # and an aspect context has no `tags` attribute.
+        if "no-check-output-for-working-dir" not in getattr(ctx.attr, "tags", []):
+            args.process_wrapper_flags.add_all(
+                checked_outputs,
+                before_each = "--check-output-for-working-dir",
+                expand_directories = False,
+            )
 
